From: Niklas Cassel <cassel@kernel.org>
Subject: [PATCH] ata: libata-core: disable LPM for Crucial BX SSD1 models

Backport the Crucial BX SSD1 family quirk to the vendor 4.1 kernel,
which does not yet have the older individual BX model entries either.
These drives can time out when link power management is enabled.

The upstream model pattern includes CT2000BX500SSD1. Leave NCQ, queue
depth, link speed and unrelated drive models unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/1066fe825987da007669d7c25306b4dbb50bd7dd]
Signed-off-by: Niklas Cassel <cassel@kernel.org>
---
 drivers/ata/libata-core.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ata/libata-core.c b/drivers/ata/libata-core.c
--- a/drivers/ata/libata-core.c
+++ b/drivers/ata/libata-core.c
@@ -4218,6 +4218,9 @@
 	{ "PIONEER DVD-RW  DVR-212D",	NULL,	ATA_HORKAGE_NOSETXFER },
 	{ "PIONEER DVD-RW  DVR-216D",	NULL,	ATA_HORKAGE_NOSETXFER },
 
+	/* Crucial devices with broken LPM support */
+	{ "CT*0BX*00SSD1",		NULL,	ATA_HORKAGE_NOLPM },
+
 	/* devices that don't properly handle queued TRIM commands */
 	{ "Micron_M500_*",		NULL,	ATA_HORKAGE_NO_NCQ_TRIM |
 						ATA_HORKAGE_ZERO_AFTER_TRIM, },
